# Trainer publish

An imported profile stays `draft` until the trainer confirms a mailbox or a Belarus mobile. Mailbox confirmation is the letter sent to the address they typed, or Google or Yandex on the same short link. A mobile confirmation is the SMS code on that same short link. Opening `/hi/{code}` alone does not publish the card. The trainer can hide the page from the cabinet. A later confirmation does not publish a hidden or archived card.

## Either channel is enough

The two confirmation channels are a mailbox and a Belarus mobile. They work as either-or. One confirmed channel activates the account. Both may be confirmed later; that does not replace the first.

The admin trainer lists (`/admin/trainers`, drafts, active, unclear) column «Аккаунт» shows only the value that first confirmed the account: the mailbox or the Belarus mobile, with no «Почта» or «Телефон» label. When both are confirmed later, the earlier one stays. No account yet is «Аккаунт не создан». An account with neither channel confirmed is «не подтверждён».

Import, a server copy, the short-link visit, and the password step do not publish it. The confirmed mailbox or the confirmed mobile does.

## Do

- Save and sync an imported profile as `draft`.
- Publish the draft when the confirmation letter is opened, Google or Yandex binds the card, or the SMS code on the short link is accepted.
- Leave the account window on the short link until the card has an owner.
- Let the trainer set the page to hidden in the cabinet.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: both channels, and a label in front of each
lines.push(`Почта ${email}`);
lines.push(`Телефон ${phone}`);

// right: one value, the channel that confirmed the account first
return confirmedAccountValue(account);
```

```ts
// wrong: the short-link visit publishes the draft
if (!staff && row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}

// right: the mailbox confirmation publishes a draft, and a hidden card stays hidden
if (row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}
```
